      <p class="lead-text">
        Before a landlord hands over store keys or a corporate client signs your consulting agreement, they will almost always ask for one thing first: proof of Commercial General Liability (CGL) insurance. It is the baseline coverage that pays legal bills and settlements when an outsider claims your business injured them or damaged their property.
      </p>

      <h2>Average General Liability Insurance Costs by Industry (2026 Data)</h2>
      <p>
        Underwriters price general liability around three numbers: your industry class code, your gross annual revenue, and your payroll. Here is what small businesses typically pay across common sectors:
